## Key JD insights

- The role's true mandate is stated outright: "remove the CEO from delivery decisions, implementation involvement and engineering bottlenecks." This is an operating-shape problem (a founder-CEO who is still the delivery bottleneck), not a feature-factory PM hire. The winning pitch is "I can be the senior person who absorbs all of that off you," which maps onto Nick running AccessBuddy solo end to end and authoring + presenting the LIMSOC national strategy without handholding.
- It is genuinely a hybrid role, not pure product. The JD repeatedly pairs product thinking with technical credibility: "lead an engineering manager," "review architecture decisions and challenge scope," "credible conversations with engineers." Nick's engineering depth (ANZ generative AI, Macquarie architecture lead) is not optional colour here, it is a hard requirement and a real differentiator.
- The company is a B2B SaaS for mining contractors, scaling fast into Enterprise and "building AI driven features, dashboards, and workflows... agentic AI development." Nick's ANZ generative-AI work and AccessBuddy AI-assisted build are directly on-thesis, which makes the technical-credibility requirement land naturally rather than as a stretch.
- The role owns ALL delivery functions: roadmap, EM, Support Lead, complex Enterprise implementations end to end, delivery process governance (cadence, release, QA, post-implementation review), and resourcing recommendations. This breadth favours someone who has owned the whole delivery surface, which is exactly the AccessBuddy (solo end-to-end) + scrum-master (2 to 6 squads, cadence and standards) + LSV (operating model, governance, decision rights) combination.
- The JD explicitly invites a rationale: "Submit your resume, along with a short rationale of what makes you the obvious choice. Applications with this written piece will be particularly well regarded." This licenses a confident, direct mapping close in the cover letter and rewards the candidate who states the fit plainly rather than generically.
- Salary band is published ($135k to $150k base) and there is a portal question on expected base, so the comp answer should be specific and sit inside or at the top of the band given Nick's seniority.
- Seek flags Nick as a "Strong applicant match" and this is the top-priority application, so the written piece should be the most explicit and confident of the batch in mapping JD core to lived evidence.

## What to target from the JD

- **Own and publish the rolling product roadmap, prioritised against company strategy and client needs** — map: LSV national scaling strategy, roadmap and national vision, prioritisation framework.
- **Be the senior technical leadership hire who removes the CEO from delivery decisions, implementation involvement and engineering bottlenecks** — map: AccessBuddy solo end-to-end ownership; LIMSOC strategy authored and presented to national executive without handholding.
- **Sufficient technical depth to lead an engineering manager, review architecture decisions and challenge scope** — map: ANZ senior engineer on generative AI platform; Macquarie solution architecture lead through platform architecture review.
- **Lead complex, multi-stakeholder Enterprise client implementations as the most senior internal person in the room** — map: LSV operating model across 8 jurisdictions; national water safety policy bringing every state into agreement.
- **Define and govern delivery processes: engineering cadences, release management, QA standards, post-implementation review** — map: scrum master scaling 2 to 6 squads; engineering standards adopted across all 6 teams; TDD, coverage enforcement, observability at Macquarie.
- **Experience scaling delivery operations as a business grows, building process and tooling that outlasts the individual** — map: Leidos 2-to-6-squad scale-up with standards adopted org-wide.
- **B2B SaaS environment, growth startup, comfortable in startup flexibility and calm pragmatic problem solving** — map: AccessBuddy live B2B SaaS as solo founder; ambiguous-environment track record.
- **Building AI driven features and agentic AI on a complex operational environment** — map: ANZ generative AI / Vertex AI / Gemini; AI-assisted product build.
- **Familiarity with but not inflexible adherence to agile delivery methodologies** — map: Certified Scrum Master, scrum master practice scaled, agile not dogmatic.
- **Translate strategic goals into a prioritised, executable roadmap the engineering team can deliver against** — map: LSV strategy plus years delivering against backlogs as the engineer, then writing them.

